# The lexer's reports a `use` line's path takes back (defect 2391). The lexer
# runs before the parser and knows no `use` line, so a key or a version inside
# a path, `2e3` in a placed tree's key `2e3e1bba9c8acea1`, is told as a number
# before the parser tells the whole path as one mistake, an address or a placed
# tree's folder (`package_mark.told_whole`, the codes `use_holds_an_address`
# and `package_unmarked`). Where it does, a report the lexer made inside that
# path is a second message for the one mistake and is taken back; a report
# reaching past the path is kept. A report at the word a mark holds where
# the entry's name stands is taken back too, `let` in `use <let>/x`, which
# the parser tells with the entry (`package_wants_a_name`, defect 2432) and
# the lexer told as a binding, `x = 5`; and so is a refused word where a
# path's part or its alias stands, `let` in `use a/let`, which the parser
# tells at the word (`use_told.hero`, defect 2451). The parser applies it where it applies
# `unclosed.withdrawn` (`parse.hero`), for the strict and the control arm alike.
#
# Split from `package_mark.hero` at its line ceiling
# (`tests/harness/suite_layout.hero`), along the seam of whose report a path
# keeps, apart from how a mark is read.

use diag
use token

# The lexer's reports `lexed` keeps where `said` holds the parser's: every one
# but those inside a path the parser told whole.
function withdrawn(lexed: [diag.Diagnostic], said: [diag.Diagnostic]) -> [diag.Diagnostic]
    out: [diag.Diagnostic] @= []

    for d in lexed
        if !inside_a_path(said, span: d.span) && !word_retold(said, lexed: d)
            out @ out.push(d)

    return out

# Whether `span` lies inside a path the parser told whole.
function inside_a_path(said: [diag.Diagnostic], span: token.Span) -> bool
    for d in said
        whole = d.code == "use_holds_an_address" || d.code == "package_unmarked" || d.code == "package_wants_a_name"

        if whole && d.span.start <= span.start && span.end <= d.span.end
            return true

    return false

# Whether `lexed` is the lexer's report of a refused word that the parser
# told again at the same word, where a `use` line's part or alias stands
# (defect 2451: `let` in `use a/let`, told by the lexer as a binding's word):
# the report's code is `reserved_word`, the lexer's one code for such a
# word, and a parser report under one of the codes `use_told.hero` tells a
# word with stands at its very span. Both are asked, since those codes stand
# at the `use` keyword or a `/` too, where the lexer may report another
# mistake (`continuation_outside_brackets` at a `use` alone on its line).
function word_retold(said: [diag.Diagnostic], lexed: diag.Diagnostic) -> bool
    if lexed.code != "reserved_word"
        return false

    for d in said
        if d.span == lexed.span && (d.code == "expected_module_name" || d.code == "module_path_wants_a_part" || d.code == "package_wants_a_module" || d.code == "expected_alias_name")
            return true

    return false
